nt contracts and Bridge-owned cross-graph subscriptions.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/tasks/canon-templates-in-order/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#1d4ed822;color:#1d4ed8;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>C</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Canon templates in order</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Get every canon template into the current model, so that the view-shape conversion and the publish are done once, on graphs that are settled.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/tasks/canon-view-shape-consistency/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#b91c1c22;color:#b91c1c;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>T</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Twilite Zone graphs follow the view-shape rule</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Every surface in the twilite.zone canon keeps one shape: the Detail defines it, and the views behind it take it.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/tasks/chat-node-provenance/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>C</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Create the Chat Provenance Node</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden;font-size:2.6cqw;line-height:1.3;color:#64748b'>Define, implement, and validate a first-class Chat node that preserves an originating conversation as explicit graph provenance.</span></span></a><a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/tasks/edge-class-consumes-stroke-control/root.node' style='display:flex;gap:2.2cqw;align-items:flex-start;box-sizing:border-box;height:14.2cqw;padding:1.6cqw 2.1cqw;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:2.4cqw;background:#f8fafc;text-decoration:none;color:inherit;min-width:0;overflow:hidden'><span style='flex:none;width:6.2cqw;height:6.2cqw;border-radius:1.6cqw;background:#6d28d922;color:#6d28d9;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:600;font-size:3cqw'>M</span><span style='min-width:0'><span style='display:block;font-weight:600;font-size:2.9cqw;line-height:1.25;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;color:#0f172a'>Make the Edge Class Consume Stroke Controls</span><span style='display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webk